# Force LF line endings on checkout for all text, regardless of the puller's git
# core.autocrlf or the OS/tooling used to transfer the repo (e.g. Windows/MobaXterm).
# Rationale (learned 2026-07-03 on the robot):
#   - CRLF in an executed script's shebang makes the kernel look for 'python3\r'
#     -> `/usr/bin/env: 'python3\r': No such file or directory` (roslaunch exit 127).
# This pins CHECKOUT to LF so a robot pulling through Windows/autocrlf gets byte-identical
# LF scripts. NOTE: the ROS python nodes/launch are LF in the repo; only they need this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# EXEMPTION: the sonar-vendor reloc kernel was vendored VERBATIM with Windows CRLF, and
# CHECKSUMS.sha256 / assert_vendored_checksums are anchored to those exact CRLF bytes. These
# files are imported / run via `python3 <file>` (never shebang-executed), so CRLF is harmless
# to execution. Mark them -text so git NEVER normalizes them in either direction -- keeps the
# byte-for-byte vendored copy and its checksums valid even under `git add --renormalize`.
sonar_slam/scripts/reloc/*.py -text

# Never normalize binaries (point clouds, maps, images, bags, compiled objects).
*.pcd  binary
*.pgm  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.bag  binary
*.pyc  binary
*.so   binary
*.a    binary
*.o    binary
